A send that fails must not be silent.

MONEYMONEY NEVER LEAVES ITS SPLASH, and the reason is one line that nothing ever printed.

trustd receives the trust evaluation, runs it, gets kSecTrustResultUnspecified and calls
xpc_connection_send_message with the reply. Its own log then says it replied. The application waits
for that reply forever.

handle_send_result is where the truth was: every caller ignores its return value, and the only
report of a failed send is an xpc_log_debug that has no sink in this container. A send that failed
and a send that arrived looked exactly the same from outside the process.

With this trace on, the failing run says

    CIDER_XPC send FAILED reason=4 err=0x10000002 id=0x10000000 dest=0xb03

reason 4 is DISPATCH_MACH_MESSAGE_SEND_FAILED and 0x10000002 is MACH_SEND_INVALID_DATA, which
ipc_kmsg_get returns when copyinmsg cannot read the message out of the sending process. The daemon
was alive and logging at that moment.

DEFERRED IS NOT DELIVERED and is called out separately: DISPATCH_MACH_NEEDS_DEFERRED_SEND leaves the
message queued on the channel, and a daemon that exits right after replying takes the queue with it.

Gated on a NON-EMPTY CIDER_TRACE_XPC, unlike the older traces in this file: drivers here export
every switch empty, so getenv != NULL is true in every run.
--- a/src/connection.m
+++ b/src/connection.m
@@ -101,6 +101,30 @@
 
 // returns `true` if there was no error, `false` otherwise
 static bool handle_send_result(dispatch_mach_msg_t message, dispatch_mach_reason_t sendResult, mach_error_t sendError, bool expecting_reply) {
+	/*
+	 * A SEND THAT FAILS IS SILENT: every caller of this ignores the return, and the only report is
+	 * an xpc_log_debug that goes nowhere. That is indistinguishable from a delivered message, which
+	 * is exactly the question when a daemon logs that it replied and its client waits forever.
+	 */
+	{
+		const char* trace = getenv("CIDER_TRACE_XPC");
+
+		if (trace != NULL && trace[0] != '\0') {
+			mach_msg_header_t* header = message ? dispatch_mach_msg_get_msg(message, NULL) : NULL;
+			bool sent = sendResult == DISPATCH_MACH_MESSAGE_SENT;
+
+			/* DEFERRED is not delivered: it is queued on the channel, and a daemon that exits
+			 * right after replying takes the queue with it. */
+			fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_XPC send %s reason=%lu err=0x%x id=0x%x dest=0x%x%s\n",
+			        sent ? "SENT" : (sendResult == DISPATCH_MACH_NEEDS_DEFERRED_SEND ? "DEFERRED" : "FAILED"),
+			        (unsigned long) sendResult, (unsigned) sendError,
+			        header ? (unsigned) header->msgh_id : 0u,
+			        header ? (unsigned) header->msgh_remote_port : 0u,
+			        expecting_reply ? " (expecting reply)" : "");
+			fflush(stderr);
+		}
+	}
+
 	switch (sendResult) {
 		case DISPATCH_MACH_MESSAGE_SENT: {
 			xpc_log_debug(connection, "message%s successfully sent", expecting_reply ? " expecting reply" : "");
